    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d323">

                <pb facs="0619" n="609" xml:id="pg609"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/12–1146: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-12-11">December 11,
                        1946</date>.<lb/>[Received December 11—6:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2083. Summary. Special Ministry [of] Information press conference December
                    9th:</p>
                <p>George Yeh, Foreign Office spokesman, confirmed Chinese press reports Government
                    plans to send official emissary to Yenan to discuss resumption peace talks
                    “under consideration.” No decision made on who will represent Government.
                    Pressed further by correspondents, Yeh insisted final decision to send emissary
                    not been made.</p>
                <p>(Chinese press reports indicate Chang Chun, Foreign Minister Wang Shih Chieh and
                    Shao Li Tze<anchor n="11" xml:id="d323-f1"/> under consideration as Government
                    delegate.)</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d323-f1" n="11" xml:id="d323-f1-content">
                <p>Secretary General of the Chinese People’s Political Council.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
